redfin 1247: boot-arg sweettouchid=N applies the tested Touch ID switch set at boot, persona last (default: nothing)

One switch instead of the PC bring-up (tid-bringup5.sh). Bit 0: 2 s after sweet_ufs init a thread call writes,
through the sysctl handlers, kern.sweet_fpc 3, sweet_passcode 1 (bit 2: 3; skipped with boot-arg sweetpasscode),
sweet_fb_sleep_blank 1, sweet_rpmb 1, sweet_mesa_match 2, sweet_mesa_catacomb 7, sweet_mesa_offline 1,
sweet_passcode_biostate 1, sweet_mesa_fix 0x17, sweet_mesa_lockout 0xf, sweet_passcode_bio_buzz 0x7f000c,
(bit 1: sweet_mesa_wake 5), sweet_mesa_fwd_wait_ms 15000, sweet_mesa_reload 1, and last kern.sweet_mesa 3, so
biometrickitd's IOKit launch event fires with every switch already set (no "mesa 0, then 3 + kill" dance).
All stay normal sysctls. kern.sweet_touchid_boot (RO) lists what was applied and each errno.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC4dCbJuYfzxCtCk4D8
